# XSH isinf()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#

assertion  XSH.isinf.001
anchor     functions/isinf.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/isinf.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       isinf() of +Inf and -Inf is non-zero, for each of the three floating
           types.
test       t/001-infinite.c

assertion  XSH.isinf.002
anchor     functions/isinf.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/isinf.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       isinf() of 0, -0, 1, MAX, -MAX, a NaN and its negation is 0, for each
           of the three floating types.
test       t/002-not-infinite.c

assertion  XSH.isinf.003
anchor     functions/isinf.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/isinf.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       For float and double, isinf(MAX * 2), with MAX the largest finite
           value of the type, is non-zero: a product evaluated in a wider format
           is converted to the semantic type first.
test       t/003-semantic-type.c
